INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Public attribution and blockchain-analysis sources on Ronin and Harmony Horizon thefts", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002; SRC-003; SRC-004", "text": "Evidence returned by benchmark tools: SRC-001 (Elliptic, May 9 2023) says the FBI confirmed North Korea-backed Lazarus Group was behind the June 2022 Harmony Horizon Bridge hack; Horizon was exploited for $99.7M on June 24, 2022. Elliptic says the funds were programmatically structured through Tornado Cash, and that the laundering methods mirrored those used for the Ronin Bridge hack. It estimates more than $555M from the two hacks went through Tornado Cash: more than $468M from Ronin and $96M from Harmony. It says post-Tornado funds were dormant until Jan. 2023, then structured into Railgun; about 70% of ETH sent through Railgun was estimated to be Harmony-hack funds, followed by deposits into Binance and Huobi, which announced blocking/seizing part of the funds. SRC-003 (Elliptic, Mar. 29 2022) says Ronin disclosed theft of 173,600 ETH and 25.5M USDC, worth $540M at theft; on Apr. 14 2022 OFAC sanctioned the exploiter Ethereum address and listed its owner as Lazarus Group. It says the attacker obtained 5 of 9 validator keys, swapped stolen USDC for ETH via DEXs, sent $16.7M ETH through three centralized exchanges, then used Tornado Cash after exchanges announced cooperation with law enforcement; $80.3M ETH had gone through Tornado Cash and $9.7M sat in intermediary wallets, with $433M remaining in the original wallet as of the article’s snapshot. SRC-002 (Chainalysis, Sep. 8 2022) says Lazarus gained five of nine Ronin validator keys and approved withdrawals of 173,600 ETH and 25.5M USDC; laundering leveraged over 12,000 addresses. It describes a typical North Korea-linked DeFi laundering sequence: intermediary wallets, Tornado Cash mixing, ETH-to-BTC swap, Bitcoin mixing, and crypto-to-fiat cashout. It says over $30M was seized, about 10% of stolen funds, and later chain-hopping used bridges and swaps. SRC-004 returned only a generic current Elliptic resource page and did not add substantive evidence. No benchmark source returned evidence equating Lazarus Group with APT38; do not assert that identity."}
